==German==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|de|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|de|gmh|brust}}, from {{inh|de|goh|brust}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*brust}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*brusts}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/bʁʊst/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Brust.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-Brust2.ogg|audio (Berlin)}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Brust.ogg|Audio (Austria)}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f,^e|dim=^chen}}

# [[chest]]
# [[breast]] (''of a woman''); [[side]] of the [[chest]] (''of a man'')

====Usage notes====
* While the singular of the German word is perfectly neutral with regard to natural gender, the plural {{m|de|Brüste}} is roughly equivalent to English {{m|en||breasts}} and is now rarely used to refer to (human) males.

====Declension====
{{de-ndecl|f,^e}}

